e96ed6c5d341c9b4a926?width=700&format=jpeg&auto=webp 700w, https://i.insider.com/6afde96ed6c5d341c9b4a926?width=1000&format=jpeg&auto=webp 1000w, https://i.insider.com/6afde96ed6c5d341c9b4a926?width=1300&format=jpeg&auto=webp 1300w, https://i.insider.com/6afde96ed6c5d341c9b4a926?width=2000&format=jpeg&auto=webp 2000w\" sizes=\"(min-width: 1280px) 900px\" alt=\"NEW YORK, NEW YORK - OCTOBER 5: Former Anthropic researcher Jacob Coxon testifies during a New York City Council Committee hearing on the risks and regulation of artificial intelligence at City Hall on October 5, 2026 in New York City. Top executives from OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, and Meta are testifying under oath today at an NYC Council Committee of the Whole Hearing, to address artificial intelligence safety risks and proposed municipal regulations. (Photo by Adam Gray/Getty Images)\" decoding=\"sync\">\n                        </p></div>\n                    \n                          <figcaption data-e2e-name=\"image-caption\">\n                            <details>\n                              <summary aria-label=\"Image caption\">\n                                  <span data-e2e-name=\"image-source\" itemprop=\"creditText\">Adam Gray/Getty Images</span>              </summary>\n                              <span>AI engineerJacob Coxon said he's donating his equity in OpenAI to AI safety research.</span>\n                            </details>\n                          </figcaption>\n                    </figure>\n              </div>\n    \n    \n    \n          \n    \n            <div data-e2e-name=\"post-details\">\n                \n                \n                \n                \n                  <p><time data-timestamp=\"2026-11-18T19:46:02.022Z\" data-disable-relative-formatting=\"\">\n                      2026-11-18T19:46:02.022Z\n                    </time>\n                  </p>\n              </div>\n    \n    \n          \n    \n            \n            \n            \n    \n          \n    \n      <section data-load-strategy=\"lazy\" data-component-type=\"image-modal\" data-track-content=\"\" data-post-type=\"story\" data-track-marfeel=\"post-body-content\">\n                \n                      <p><a target=\"_self\" href=\"https://www.businessinsider.com/anthropic-researcher-quits-over-ai-safety-concerns-2026-9\" data-track-click=\"{&quot;element_name&quot;:&quot;body_link&quot;,&quot;event&quot;:&quot;tout_click&quot;,&quot;index&quot;:&quot;bi_value_unassigned&quot;,&quot;product_field&quot;:&quot;bi_value_unassigned&quot;}\" rel=\"\">Jacob Coxon</a> is forking over what could be a massive personal windfall in the name of AI safety.</p><p>The ex-OpenAI researcher, who also worked at Anthropic before he recently quit, said on Wednesday that he's committed to selling his equity in OpenAI and donating the proceeds to AI safety causes.</p><p>\"We need to pause or drastically slow down the race to superintelligence,\" he said on X. \"Everything else is a distraction.\"</p><p>In doing so, Coxon is forgoing what could be millions of dollars in profit that would become liquid when <a target=\"_self\" href=\"https://www.businessinsider.com/sam-altman-openai-ipo-plan-investor-demand-2026-11\" data-track-click=\"{&quot;element_name&quot;:&quot;body_link&quot;,&quot;event&quot;:&quot;tout_click&quot;,&quot;index&quot;:&quot;bi_value_unassigned&quot;,&quot;product_field&quot;:&quot;bi_value_unassigned&quot;}\" rel=\"\">OpenAI goes public</a>, an event that CEO Sam Altman has said is on the horizon.</p><p>Coxon made serious waves in September when he left Anthropic and issued a series of dire warnings that it and OpenAI were \"gambling with our lives.\"</p><p>\"The people building AI earnestly believe that it could kill us all by the end of the decade,\" he said in an X post on September 8 that has since racked up 175 million views. \"This is not a marketing stunt.\"</p><p>Coxon worked at OpenAI from 2023 until 2026, before leaving for Anthropic. Since then, the 27-year-old from England has done the <a target=\"_self\" href=\"https://www.businessinsider.com/former-anthropic-openai-jacob-coxon-self-automatation-research-work-2026-10\" data-track-click=\"{&quot;element_name&quot;:&quot;body_link&quot;,&quot;event&quot;:&quot;tout_click&quot;,&quot;index&quot;:&quot;bi_value_unassigned&quot;,&quot;product_field&quot;:&quot;bi_value_unassigned&quot;}\" rel=\"\">rounds with media</a> to advocate for AI safeguards and, principally, a pause on recursive self-improvement, the process by which AI models train themselves.</p><p>In a November 9 talk at Stanford, Coxon called his stake in OpenAI \"blood money\" but balked at giving it up at the time.</p><p>\"I like money, bro,\" he said. \"My parents were like worried I was having a psychotic break. I think if I'd also given away all the money they'd be even more convinced of that.\"</p>\n                \n                \n                  </section>\n    \n    \n    \n    \n      </section>\n\n    \n    <!-- Included desktop \"post-aside\" -->    \n\n    \n      \n      <section data-component-type=\"post-bottom\" data-load-strategy=\"exclude\" data-track-marfeel=\"post-bottom\">\n        <section>\n    \n    \n            \n            \n    \n            \n            \n            <section data-component-type=\"read-next\" data-e2e-name=\"read-next\" data-display-size=\"4\" data-post-id=\"6afde90ba39a61840d331a8a\" data-root-margin=\"250px 0px\" data-track-view=\"{&quot;subscription_experience&quot;:&quot;bi_value_unassigned&quot;,&quot;product_field&quot;:&quot;bi_value_unassigned&quot;,&quot;element_name&quot;:&quot;end_of_article_recirc&quot;}\">\n              <h2>Read next</h2>\n            \n              <div data-track-click-shared=\"{&quot;product_field&quot;:&quot;bi_value_unassigned&quot;,&quot;event&quot;:&quot;tout_click&quot;,&quot;element_name&quot;:&quot;end_of_article_recirc&quot;,&quot;click_text&quot;:&quot;Read next&quot;}\" data-recommend